Conopodium is a genus of flowering plants belonging to the family Apiaceae.

Its native range is north-western Europe and the Mediterranean.

Species
The following species are recognised in the genus Conopodium:

Conopodium arvense {{small|(Coss.) Calest.}}
Conopodium bunioides {{small|(Boiss.) Calest.}}
Conopodium glaberrimum {{small|(Desf.) Engstrand.}}
Conopodium majus {{small|(Gouan) Loret}}
Conopodium marianum {{small|Lange}}
Conopodium pyrenaeum {{small|(Loisel.) Miégev.}}
Conopodium subcarneum {{small|(Boiss. & Reut.) Boiss.}}
Conopodium thalictrifolium {{small|(Boiss.) Calest.}}
